---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const base = '/participation-nd-long-history/20261107-01/';
type Counts = { ballots_by_year: Record<string, number>;
	reported_count_change_since: Record<string, number> };
type County = Counts & { county_name: string };
const review: { statewide: Counts; counties: County[] } =
	JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}history.json`, 'utf8'));
const years = ['2016', '2018', '2020', '2022', '2024', '2026'];
const number = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
const change = (value: number) => `${value > 0 ? '+' : ''}${number(value)}`;
---

<section id="participation-nd-long-history" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="nd-long-history-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Administrative ballot counts · six elections</p>
		<h2 id="nd-long-history-title">North Dakota participation, 2016–2026</h2>
		<p>Presidential and midterm ballot counts for all 53 counties. The five historical elections
			are official; <strong>2026 is an unofficial snapshot, not final turnout</strong>,
			updated November 5, 2026 at 01:30 UTC.
			Count changes are <strong>not measured prior-voter drop-off or switching</strong>.</p>
	</header>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Six-election North Dakota statewide ballot counts">
		<table>
			<caption>Statewide general-election ballots. Compare midterms with midterms separately
				from presidential elections; candidate votes are not substituted for ballots.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Geography</th>
				{years.map(year => <th scope="col">{year}{year === '2026' ? ' snapshot' : ' official'}</th>)}
				<th scope="col">2026 vs. 2018</th><th scope="col">2026 vs. 2020</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody><tr data-nd-long-state>
				<th scope="row">North Dakota</th>
				{years.map(year =>
					<td data-nd-long-year={year}>{number(review.statewide.ballots_by_year[year])}</td>)}
				{['2018', '2020'].map(year =>
					<td data-nd-long-change={year}>{change(review.statewide.reported_count_change_since[year])}</td>)}
			</tr></tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<details class="explorer-notes" id="nd-long-history-counties">
		<summary>All 53 counties across six elections</summary>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Six-election North Dakota county ballot counts">
			<table>
				<caption>Exact source county-name matches, not a fixed-person cohort. County totals
					are sums of complete native reporting units, not independent county controls.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">County</th>
					{years.map(year => <th scope="col">{year}{year === '2026' ? ' snapshot' : ''}</th>)}
					<th scope="col">2026 vs. 2018</th><th scope="col">2026 vs. 2020</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{review.counties.map(row => <tr data-nd-long-county={row.county_name}>
					<th scope="row">{row.county_name}</th>
					{years.map(year =>
						<td data-nd-long-year={year}>{number(row.ballots_by_year[year])}</td>)}
					{['2018', '2020'].map(year =>
						<td data-nd-long-change={year}>{change(row.reported_count_change_since[year])}</td>)}
				</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<p>The native sources contain 432, 424, 422, 398, 385 and 358 reporting units,
		respectively. The older 2016–2020 tables use <strong>named reporting units, not numeric
		precinct IDs</strong>. Names and IDs do not establish comparable precinct boundaries.
		No new precinct map, demographic turnout rate, individual drop-off or returning-voter identity is inferred.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Source definitions, clocks and complete reproduction</summary>
		<p>The <a href="https://www.sos.nd.gov/elections/election-results">North Dakota Secretary of State archive</a>
			declares the historical pages. Native update clocks are November 18, 2016 at 10:32:46 AM;
			November 20, 2018 at 10:38:27 AM; and November 12, 2020 at 3:08:14 PM.
			No historical timezone is supplied. Every later source clock remains in the complete download.</p>
		<p>Historical “Eligible Voters” means estimated residents aged 18+, not registered voters
			or a fixed eligible cohort. Those values are preserved but not used to calculate rates.
			Legacy county IDs are portal ordinals, not FIPS. Current identifiers and source clocks
			remain separate. No longitudinal precinct crosswalk or analytical boundary overlay is established.</p>
		<p>The complete archive contains all 2,419 selected reporting-unit observations, all 318
			county observations, 265 signed county count comparisons, statewide controls, all 11 used-source
			receipts, native definitions, methods, original independent source-check receipt, exact code and tests.
			It reproduces offline from complete selected facts, not metadata alone.
			Re-running initial extraction requires the pinned originals; native site code, unrelated contests
			and personal records are not redistributed. The source check does not validate individual transitions.
			This analysis is not endorsed by the source.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete six-election North Dakota inputs + code + results (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}history.json`} download>Six-election county counts + qualifications (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Six-election archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
		<a href="/participation-nd-ballot-history/20261107-01/complete-analysis.zip" download>Original three-election complete archive (unchanged)</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-nd-long-history { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
